I get the use case and advantage for use this would bring, but I'm not sure how easily this would be able to do without introducing binary breaking changes or potentially doubling the number of `ExecuteAsync()` overloads we have.

We could possibly introduce an extension method that does the same thing, but with a different name, something like the below (with an intentionally obtuse name because I can't think of a better name right now):

```csharp
public async ValueTask ExecuteWithAResilienceContextWithTheCallerNameAsTheResilienceKeyAsync(
    Func<...> callback,
    [CallerMemberName] string? callerMemberName,
    CancellationToken cancellationToken = default)
{
    var context = ResilienceContextPool.Shared.Get(callerMemberName, cancellationToken);
    try
    {
        await _connectPipeline.ExecuteAsync(callback, context).ConfigureAwait(false);
    }
    finally
    {
        ResilienceContextPool.Shared.Return(context);
    }
}
```

However, of course, if the above works, you could just add it to your own code base to minimise the amount of wrapping you need to do.

Yep, I added pretty much exactly that, but across multiple projects/repos etc. it means I have to copy this extension everywhere.

```cs
/// <summary>
/// Extensions for the Polly <see cref="ResiliencePipeline"/>.
/// </summary>
public static class ResiliencePipelineX
{
    /// <summary>
    /// Executes the specified callback in the same way as <see cref="ResiliencePipeline.ExecuteAsync(Func{CancellationToken, ValueTask}, CancellationToken)"/>,
    /// but providing the operation key automatically from the caller's name.
    /// </summary>
    /// <seealso href="https://github.com/App-vNext/Polly/issues/2755">Issue to add to Polly library.</seealso>
    /// <param name="resiliencePipeline">The <see cref="ResiliencePipeline"/> to use to execute the <paramref name="callback"/>.</param>
    /// <param name="callback">The user-provided callback.</param>
    /// <param name="cancellationToken">The <see cref="CancellationToken"/> associated with the callback.</param>
    /// <param name="operationKey">An operation key for the callback. Will default to the caller's name.</param>
    /// <returns>The instance of <see cref="ValueTask"/> that represents an asynchronous callback.</returns>
    public static async ValueTask ExecuteWithNameAsync(
        this ResiliencePipeline resiliencePipeline,
        Func<CancellationToken, ValueTask> callback,
        CancellationToken cancellationToken = default,
        [CallerMemberName] string operationKey = "")
    {
        ArgumentNullException.ThrowIfNull(resiliencePipeline);

        var context = ResilienceContextPool.Shared.Get(operationKey, cancellationToken);
        try
        {
            await resiliencePipeline.ExecuteAsync(
                context => callback(context.CancellationToken),
                context)
                .ConfigureAwait(context.ContinueOnCapturedContext);
        }
        finally
        {
            ResilienceContextPool.Shared.Return(context);
        }
    }
}
```

