Hi @lonix1 we had made the required changes and it will be available as part of the 8.5.0 release. The new property name will be `TelemetrySource` (the `Source` was already defined by the `Exception` type...). It is not a string rather a [`ResilienceTelemetrySource`](https://www.pollydocs.org/api/Polly.Telemetry.ResilienceTelemetrySource.html). This class includes not just the strategy name but information about the pipeline as well.

So, the usage will look like this:

```cs
try 
{
    await pipeline.ExecuteAsync(...);
}
catch (RateLimiterRejectedException ex) when (ex.TelemetrySource.StrategyName?.Contains("ThreadLimiter"))
{
  // Your concurrency limiter related logic
}
```

I think the issue here is that the context is per invocation of your pipeline, so every time you execute it it's a new one with no memory of what went before:

```csharp
while (true)
{
    var context = ResilienceContextPool.Shared.Get("test-resilience-context");

    try
    {
        _ = await pipeline.ExecuteAsync<HttpResponseMessage>(async (token) =>
        {

            ...
        }, context: context);
    }
    finally
    {
        ResilienceContextPool.Shared.Return(context);
    }
}
```

The state of the circuit breaker only changes once per invocation of the pipeline, which is why it always seems to not be being persisted - it _is_ being persisted, but then it's "thrown away" in the `finally` block.

If you want to keep state across invocations, you should store the state separately and set that on the context before invoking the pipeline.

Here's an example where I've adapted your original code:

```csharp
using Polly;
using Polly.CircuitBreaker;
using Polly.Fallback;

internal class Program
{
    private static readonly ResiliencePropertyKey<State> circuitOpenedContextKey = new ResiliencePropertyKey<State>("CircuitOpenedCount");

    static async Task Main(string[] args)
    {
        await TestPipelineWithResilienceContext();
    }

    record State()
    {
        public int CircuitOpenedCount { get; set; }
    }

    private static async Task TestPipelineWithResilienceContext()
    {
        var pipeline = GetPipelineWithResilienceContext();
        var client = new HttpClient() { BaseAddress = new Uri("http://internal.my-service.com/api/test") };

        var state = new State();

        while (true)
        {
            var context = ResilienceContextPool.Shared.Get("test-resilience-context");
            context.Properties.Set(circuitOpenedContextKey, state);

            try
            {
                _ = await pipeline.ExecuteAsync(async (token) =>
                {

                    var response = await client.GetAsync("test-endpoint");
                    response.EnsureSuccessStatusCode();
                    return response;
                }, context: context); // Pass context to the pipeline.
            }
            catch
            {
                // Nothing to do here. We just want to test the pipeline and check the console.                
            }
            finally
            {
                // Always send the context back to the pool.
                ResilienceContextPool.Shared.Return(context);
            }

            await Task.Delay(500);
        }
    }

    private static ResiliencePipeline<HttpResponseMessage> GetPipelineWithResilienceContext()
    {
        // Counters and limits.
        const int circuitOpenLimit = 3;

        // Create the pipeline builder.
        var builder = new ResiliencePipelineBuilder<HttpResponseMessage>();

        // Configure fallback to execute with an open circuit.
        var fallbackOptions = new FallbackStrategyOptions<HttpResponseMessage>()
        {
            ShouldHandle = static args =>
            {
                if (args.Outcome.Exception != null
                    &&
                    args.Outcome.Exception.GetType() == typeof(BrokenCircuitException))
                {
                    if (args.Context.Properties.TryGetValue(circuitOpenedContextKey, out var state) && state.CircuitOpenedCount >= circuitOpenLimit)
                    {
                        Console.WriteLine($"[{DateTime.Now.ToString("dd-MM-yyyy HH:mm:ss.fffff")}] Starting fallback due to reached open circuit count limit: {state.CircuitOpenedCount}.");
                        return PredicateResult.True();
                    }
                    else
                    {
                        Console.WriteLine($"[{DateTime.Now.ToString("dd-MM-yyyy HH:mm:ss.fffff")}] Fallback will be skipped due to unreached open circuit count limit: {state.CircuitOpenedCount}.");
                        return PredicateResult.False();
                    }
                }

