The `OnRetry` customer delegate is [being called](https://github.com/App-vNext/Polly/blob/main/src/Polly.Core/Retry/RetryResilienceStrategy.cs#L83) after an unsuccessful attempt and before the strategy goes to sleep. This has two implications which are important from the question perspective:
1. The `OnRetry` is executed after the original attempt's failure as well
2. The `OnRetry` is not executed after the last retry attempt

The below solution tries to address these problems.

## Extend the `RetryStrategyOptions`

Let's add a new customer delegate called `OnFailedRetry`
```cs
public class CustomRetryStrategyOptions<TResult>: RetryStrategyOptions<TResult>
{
    public Func<OnRetryArguments<TResult>, ValueTask>? OnFailedRetry { get; set; }
}
```
This property has the exact same signature as the `OnRetry`. If you want to use this class in your production code please rename `CustomRetryStrategyOptions` to something more meaningful 😊

## Define a custom strategy
One way to tackle the second implication (so calling automatically the `OnFailedRetry` if the last attempt failed) is to wire up a custom strategy into a resilience pipeline. 

```cs
internal sealed class LogAfterStrategy<TResult>: ResilienceStrategy<TResult>
{
    private readonly CustomRetryStrategyOptions<TResult> options;

    public LogAfterStrategy(CustomRetryStrategyOptions<TResult> options)
        => this.options = options;   

    protected override async ValueTask<Outcome<TResult>> ExecuteCore<TState>(
        Func<ResilienceContext, TState, ValueTask<Outcome<TResult>>> callback,
        ResilienceContext context,
        TState state)
    {
       	var outcome = await callback(context, state).ConfigureAwait(context.ContinueOnCapturedContext);

	var shouldRetryArgs = new RetryPredicateArguments<TResult>(context, outcome, options.MaxRetryAttempts);
        var handle = await options.ShouldHandle(shouldRetryArgs).ConfigureAwait(context.ContinueOnCapturedContext);

	if(handle)
	{
	       //ExecutionTime for the last retry is unknown so, I passed TimeSpan.Zero for that
		var args = new OnRetryArguments<TResult>(context, outcome, options.MaxRetryAttempts, TimeSpan.Zero, TimeSpan.Zero);
		await options.OnFailedRetry(args).ConfigureAwait(context.ContinueOnCapturedContext);
	}
        return outcome;
    }
}
```
The `ExecuteCore`
- executes the `callback` which is either the next resilience strategy or the decorated user callback depending on whether it is registered as an outer or as the innermost strategy (respectively) into the pipeline
- calls the `ShouldHandle` to decide whether the outcome is considered successful or unsuccessful 
  - The `handle` variable is `true` if the `outcome` is unsuccessful
- executes the `OnFailedRetry` if the `outcome` was unsuccessful
- finally it returns the `outcome`

## Wire up pipeline

We want to execute the `OnFailedRetry` customer delegate after the retry strategy exhausted all of its attempts. That means the `LogAfterStrategy` should be the outer strategy and a retry should be the inner.

```cs
public static class RetryExtensions
{ 
    public static ResiliencePipelineBuilder<TResult> AddCustomRetry<TResult>(this ResiliencePipelineBuilder<TResult> builder, CustomRetryStrategyOptions<TResult> options)
    {
        return builder
	.AddStrategy(context => new LogAfterStrategy<TResult>(options), options)
        .AddRetry(new() {
            BackoffType = options.BackoffType,
            Delay = options.Delay,
            DelayGenerator = options.DelayGenerator,
	    MaxDelay = options.MaxDelay,
            MaxRetryAttempts = options.MaxRetryAttempts,
	    ShouldHandle = options.ShouldHandle,
            UseJitter = options.UseJitter,
            OnRetry = async args =>
            {
			if(options.OnRetry is {})
			{
				await options.OnRetry(args).ConfigureAwait(args.Context.ContinueOnCapturedContext);
			}
				
			if(options.OnFailedRetry is {} && args.AttemptNumber > 0)
			{
				await options.OnFailedRetry(args).ConfigureAwait(args.Context.ContinueOnCapturedContext);
			}
            }
        });
    }
}
```
- The [registration order does matter](https://www.pollydocs.org/pipelines/index.html#diagrams) so, first we register the `LogAfter` then the `Retry` strategy
- The retry registration does the following things
  - it maps the `CustomRetryStrategyOptions` properties to the `RetryStrategyOptions` properties
  - it executes the `OnRetry` if it is defined
  - it executes the `OnFailedRetry` if it is defined and it was not the original attempt 
    - _this addresses the first implication_ 
- To encapsulate these strategies bundling we can create a simple extension method (`AddCustomRetry`)

