Having read your proposal, I don't fully understand what problem you're trying to solve here with regards to Polly itself.

The [`IReadOnlyPolicyRegistry<TKey>`](https://github.com/App-vNext/Polly/blob/master/src/Polly/Registry/IReadOnlyPolicyRegistry.cs) interface(s) provide a way to access previously created policies, which can be registered with DI itself.

The registry is there to provide a way for policies to be reused across requests. Examples of this usage are for circuit-breakers. If you don't reuse them across all your requests then one individual request will likely never hit the configured limits for the circuit breaker to open, making it not behave as intended. Similarly with the bulkhead policy.

If you registered the registry with your DI container and took it as a dependency in your service where you want to use it, it would be scope agnostic and be (re)created as appropriate by the scopes related to the DI container.

