@shagilt Short answer: The `Polly.Context` which is scoped to (unique to) each execution is passed to the `onRetryAsync`.  And the retry count is also passed to the `onRetryAsync`.  So, in the `onRetryAsync`, you can capture on `Polly.Context` how many retries were used:

    context["retriesUsed"] = retryCount;

You could then have a custom `DelegatingHandler` configured outside the PolicyHandlers, which can use: 

    var context = requestMessage.GetPolicyExecutionContext();

to get the `Polly.Context` _after_ delegating to `base.SendAsync(...)`. If `context["retriesUsed"]` is set, retries have been used, and that can be logged.  

As you want only to log that when the execution succeeded overall, you might also need to check the `HttpResponseMessage` for success/failure status before logging.

There's a fairly [similar example here in our Polly and HttpClientFactory documentation](https://github.com/App-vNext/Polly/wiki/Polly-and-HttpClientFactory#use-case-exchanging-information-between-policy-execution-and-calling-code)

