Hi @jvitkauskas .  This can be achieved with existing Polly by [using `Polly.Context` to pass data (in this case execution duration) between the delegate executed through the policy and the `sleepDurationProvider` delegate](https://github.com/App-vNext/Polly/wiki/Keys-And-Context-Data#using-context-for-custom-data).  

Execute through the policy using an [`.Execute/Async(...)` overload taking a `Context` input parameter](https://github.com/App-vNext/Polly/blob/eff944e005ba3e39c22f4f00e60b07baf57165ec/src/Polly/AsyncPolicy.TResult.ExecuteOverloads.cs#L40), and store the execution duration in `context`:

    var context = new Context();
    var result = policy.ExecuteAsync(ctx => {
            var stopwatch = System.Diagnostics.Stopwatch.StartNew();
            try
            {
                return await action(); // the code originally intended to be executed through the policy
            }
            finally
            {
                 ctx["executionDuration"] = stopwatch.Elapsed;
            }
        }, context);

If you don't like the extra boilerplate, you can wrap it in an extension method.  Or just use the [TimingPolicy we provide on Polly.Contrib](https://github.com/Polly-Contrib/Polly.Contrib.TimingPolicy) configured something like: `timingPublisher: (span, context) => { context["executionDuration"] = span; return Task.CompletedTask; }` - you'd use that TimingPolicy inside the retry policy in a PolicyWrap.  

Meanwhile, your retry policy would be configured using [an overload where `sleepDurationProvider` takes `Context` as an input parameter](https://github.com/App-vNext/Polly/blob/eff944e005ba3e39c22f4f00e60b07baf57165ec/src/Polly/Retry/AsyncRetrySyntax.cs#L596) (just an example overload, there are similar for all variants of retry).  In the `sleepDurationProvider` just extract the execution time from `context["executionDuration"]` and make whatever calculation you want based on it.

Please let me know if that helps.  (This is a sketch to get you a quick reply rather than leave you waiting, you might need to vary some details if I overlooked anything.)

Thanks

