So I'll post my try of an explanation of this issue:
.NET limits the http client to 2 web requests by default. Why a connection is only disposed once the response is disposed might or might not be a bug.

Hence, this retry loop fails on the 3rd attempt, as 2 connections are already used.
You could set this: HttpWebRequest.ServicePoint.ConnectionLimit to a very large number, or add this to the app.config:
