Looking at the code: Polly does offer Execute overloads which take a `CancellationToken`, such as [this one](https://github.com/App-vNext/Polly/blob/4db50346299f62c2373ceba99d2522a8171c9e27/src/Polly/Policy.ExecuteOverloads.cs#L44-L53). These overloads allow the policy to respond to the token natively, so if you use such an overload, you could omit this from your `onRetry` delegate:

            if (cancellationToken.IsCancellationRequested)
            {
                logger.LogWarning("  !!! Request for graceful shutdown - so we're going to stop trying ....");
                throw new OperationCanceledException();
            }

and execute through the policy instead like this: 

```
DatabaseStatistics existingDatabaseStatistics = null;
try
{
    var checkRavenDbPolicy = policy ?? CheckRavenDbPolicy(cancellationToken, logger);
    checkRavenDbPolicy.Execute(token =>
    {
        existingDatabaseStatistics = documentStore.Maintenance.Send(new GetStatisticsOperation());
    }, cancellationToken);
}
catch (DatabaseDoesNotExistException)
{
    existingDatabaseStatistics = null; // No statistics because there's no Db tenant.
}
catch (AuthorizationException)
{
    // We failed to authenticate against the database. This _usually_ means that we
    // probably didn't have ADMIN rights against a db (so we can't do high level stuff)
    // but we could still do other stuff, like add fake data for seeding the DB.
    // SUMMARY: Db Tenant might exist, so lets assume that it does (safer bet).
    existingDatabaseStatistics = new DatabaseStatistics();
}
catch (OperationCanceledException oce) when (oce.CancellationToken == cancellationToken)
{
    logger.LogWarning("  !!! Request for graceful shutdown - so we stopped trying ....");
}
```

(The changes are to pass the `cancellationToken` local variable into the Execute call, and to move the logging which was originally in the `onRetry` - not necessarily better; just sharing options)

We do have [extensive tests on sync retry policies responding to cancellation](https://github.com/App-vNext/Polly/blob/4db50346299f62c2373ceba99d2522a8171c9e27/src/Polly.Specs/Retry/RetrySpecs.cs#L414-L771), so if you can get the token to signal, the policy will respond.

I hope that this is useful.

