To clarify:

>Based on the Timeout Policy documentation, it seems that Timeout Policy will cause a synchronous task to be put on a separate thread and abandoned if the timeout is hit

That is specific to [`TimeoutStrategy.Pessimistic` for synchronous executions](https://github.com/App-vNext/Polly/wiki/Timeout#additional-notes-pessimistic-timeout-for-sync-executions) only.  To see the difference, if you change the declaration of the policy in the above example to:

    var timeoutPolicy = Policy.Timeout(TimeSpan.FromSeconds(4.5), TimeoutStrategy.Pessimistic);

then you will see instead the behaviour stated as undesirable in your case - that the policy makes the calling thread walk away from waiting for execution after 4.5 seconds.

